WEBVTT

00:07.870 --> 00:11.020
<i>No one is unluckier than Misumi Makoto.</i>

00:11.410 --> 00:13.750
<i>Though many have been sent to other worlds,</i>

00:13.750 --> 00:16.400
<i>the goddess of this one 
is an absolute she-devil.</i>

00:17.030 --> 00:22.460
<i>Many moons have passed since I came to this 
isekai and began trying to improve the world.</i>

00:22.830 --> 00:27.170
<i>With only my attentive 
demihuman family to lean on,</i>

00:27.590 --> 00:33.030
<i>my journey to trace the steps of my 
parents who once lived here continues.</i>

00:33.510 --> 00:38.670
<i>Making a living as a merchant,</i>

00:38.670 --> 00:48.860
<i>we head to Rotsgard Academy 
to open a new store.</i>

01:16.050 --> 01:18.590
<b>Season Two</b>

02:22.990 --> 02:26.830
<b></b>Town of Obitt

02:22.990 --> 02:26.830
<b></b>Town of Obitt

02:27.040 --> 02:31.420
<b>Night One   What? Moon over the Ruined Castle?</b>

02:27.040 --> 02:31.420
<b>Night One   What? Moon over the Ruined Castle?</b>

02:27.310 --> 02:29.990
Walking sure is tiring, isn't it?

02:30.480 --> 02:36.380
But it beats using a teleportation 
circle and being found by the goddess.

02:31.420 --> 02:36.050
<b>Shiki
Makoto's Follower
(Former Lich)</b>

02:36.830 --> 02:41.070
If we're not careful, we could find 
ourselves thrown into a battlefield.

02:41.070 --> 02:44.070
It's all that shit goddess's fault.

02:44.070 --> 02:46.840
We're nearly at Rotsgard.

02:47.330 --> 02:49.590
I'll find us a room.

02:49.590 --> 02:52.500
Why don't you get something 
to eat, Young Master?

02:53.450 --> 02:55.530
Anywhere is fine.

02:55.530 --> 02:56.500
Anywhere?!

02:56.500 --> 02:58.140
No, "anywhere" will not do!

02:58.140 --> 03:01.150
What would Tomoe-sama and 
Mio-sama, who await our return

03:01.150 --> 03:04.840
in the demiplane, say if I allowed 
you to stay at a cheap inn?

03:07.530 --> 03:09.580
<i>Tomoe and Mio, huh?</i>

03:09.960 --> 03:14.190
<i>I wonder if it was okay to leave the 
demiplane in their hands while I'm gone.</i>

03:14.540 --> 03:19.130
<b>Tomoe
Makoto's Follower
(Former Greater Dragon)</b>

03:14.880 --> 03:16.020
I see.

03:16.020 --> 03:18.740
I understand your recent interest in cooking

03:18.740 --> 03:23.270
and the desire to someday demonstrate 
your skills for the young master.

03:20.920 --> 03:25.510
<b>Mio
Makoto's Follower
(Former Black Spider of Disaster)</b>

03:24.990 --> 03:29.570
So you decided to cook 
something for some friends.

03:25.890 --> 03:27.850
<b></b>Emma
 Highland Orc

03:27.850 --> 03:29.810
<b></b>Beren
 Elder Dwarf

03:29.570 --> 03:31.460
What are your thoughts 
on this dreadful sight?

03:29.810 --> 03:31.770
<b></b>Komoe
 Fragment of Tomoe
(Second Generation)

03:31.760 --> 03:34.270
I'm not sure what you expect me to say.

03:34.270 --> 03:37.940
I was right to assign food 
tasters to the young master.

03:37.940 --> 03:39.430
Food tasters?

03:39.430 --> 03:44.930
I simply prepared... curry rice? 
According to the young master's memories.

03:45.740 --> 03:48.590
Have you ever eaten curry rice?

03:48.590 --> 03:52.460
Of course not. It's a 
dish from another world.

03:52.700 --> 03:55.220
Did you ask the young master how to make it?

03:55.220 --> 03:58.410
No. After all, it was 
meant to be a surprise.

03:58.800 --> 04:02.190
M-Mio-sama, this green stuff...

04:02.480 --> 04:05.640
It's mineral ore, isn't it?

04:05.640 --> 04:07.120
Yes.

04:06.430 --> 04:07.600
<b>Of course
 it is</b>

04:08.900 --> 04:13.470
It looked delicious in the 
young master's memories.

04:13.470 --> 04:17.180
That's a soft emerald,

04:17.180 --> 04:19.960
a rare mineral found in the Wasteland.

04:19.960 --> 04:25.030
The green ingredients used in curry are 
probably bell peppers or asparagus.

04:25.970 --> 04:27.650
The pot handle, too...

04:28.480 --> 04:29.660
Oh, my.

04:30.370 --> 04:32.300
The pot melted.

04:32.300 --> 04:33.620
You're gonna eat that?

04:34.160 --> 04:37.090
This didn't turn out as good as I hoped.

04:38.340 --> 04:40.670
But is it really so agonizingly bad?

04:40.670 --> 04:41.660
Mio...

04:42.300 --> 04:47.170
Most creatures of the demiplane,
the young master included, don't eat minerals.

04:47.170 --> 04:48.140
What?

04:48.140 --> 04:50.240
Rather, they cannot.

04:50.240 --> 04:52.740
Nor can they consume 
armaments or structures.

04:52.740 --> 04:53.480
What?

04:53.730 --> 04:56.440
Those aren't cooking ingredients?

04:56.440 --> 05:01.030
For you, everything in this world is food.

05:01.420 --> 05:04.300
Have you even devoted any 
time to studying cooking?

05:04.300 --> 05:06.310
I know how to use a flame.

05:06.700 --> 05:09.520
Then brown this bread for me,

05:10.150 --> 05:12.880
the way Emma serves it at meals.

05:13.520 --> 05:14.870
You mean toast, don't you?

05:14.870 --> 05:16.980
That simply involves scorching 
bread over a low flame.

05:17.830 --> 05:20.590
That's a rather sinister-looking low flame.

05:21.490 --> 05:23.060
But why?!

05:23.060 --> 05:26.560
Cooking, huh? You've got a long way to go.

05:27.740 --> 05:29.570
<i>Blue meat?</i>

05:34.050 --> 05:35.920
<i>What is this texture?</i>

05:35.920 --> 05:39.610
Come on, man. Your face 
is sour enough already.

05:39.610 --> 05:42.210
Can't you at least act like 
you're enjoying your meal?

05:42.210 --> 05:45.480
<i>Forgive me. It has a unique texture,
 but it tastes good.</i>

05:45.480 --> 05:46.150
What?

05:46.490 --> 05:47.990
Magic writing?

05:48.640 --> 05:51.680
<i>For reasons, I cannot speak Common.</i>

05:51.680 --> 05:52.460
Huh.

05:53.100 --> 05:55.580
<i>It's because of that shit goddess.</i>

05:57.250 --> 06:00.780
<i>So is this dish made using slimes?</i>

06:00.780 --> 06:02.880
How'd you know?

06:03.190 --> 06:05.880
You must be a pretty decent adventurer.

06:05.880 --> 06:07.380
<i>I thought so.</i>

06:07.780 --> 06:10.890
<i>I guess slimes are pretty tasty after all.</i>

06:11.360 --> 06:14.040
I've submitted a hunting 
request to the guild.

06:14.040 --> 06:16.520
If you're an adventurer, I'd appreciate 
it if you caught some for me.

06:17.160 --> 06:21.030
<i>I'm registered with the guild, 
but I work primarily as a merchant.</i>

06:21.480 --> 06:24.240
<i>I'm traveling from Tsige to Rotsgard.</i>

06:25.300 --> 06:27.490
That's quite the long journey.

06:30.850 --> 06:33.150
<i>Thanks for the meal. Keep the change.</i>

06:34.050 --> 06:36.150
A gold coin? Hey!

06:36.450 --> 06:37.940
Are you sure?

06:37.940 --> 06:40.110
<i>I'm out of small change.</i>

06:40.640 --> 06:43.050
<i>Does this make me a bad merchant?</i>

06:43.870 --> 06:45.460
Look at his face.

06:45.460 --> 06:46.870
It's dreadful.

06:46.870 --> 06:47.710
How tragic.

06:47.710 --> 06:49.140
He must be a demihuman.

06:49.140 --> 06:50.670
There's no way he's hyuman.

06:50.670 --> 06:51.710
Perhaps he's cursed.

06:52.010 --> 06:56.370
<i>I know I decided to stop wearing my mask, 
but I don't feel comfortable.</i>

06:57.230 --> 07:00.760
<i>But compared to the first time 
I visited a hyuman town,</i>

07:01.130 --> 07:03.190
<i>this is way more tolerable.</i>

07:03.190 --> 07:04.330
Huh? What?

07:04.330 --> 07:04.980
Terrifying!

07:10.480 --> 07:15.070
You completed a special rank job 
when you're Level 1, Rank E?

07:15.290 --> 07:16.480
Rank E?

07:16.480 --> 07:17.820
Level 1?

07:17.060 --> 07:19.780
<i>Please don't mention my rank or level.</i>

07:19.780 --> 07:22.030
<i>For some reason, they never go up.</i>

07:25.400 --> 07:27.620
<i>So the slime-hunting job is Rank B.</i>

07:28.100 --> 07:30.390
<i>I can't take it on at Rank E.</i>

07:30.390 --> 07:33.590
I told you, Moon over the 
Ruined Castle is attacking!

07:34.060 --> 07:37.300
<i>"Moon over the Ruined Castle"?
I love that song.</i>

07:37.690 --> 07:39.310
<i>What does she mean by "it's attacking"?</i>

07:39.540 --> 07:41.510
I'm prepared to offer a reward.

07:41.510 --> 07:43.860
Why won't anyone do anything?

07:43.860 --> 07:45.560
No one can do anything right away.

07:46.230 --> 07:48.210
They're brutal bandits.

07:48.210 --> 07:49.910
They have over a hundred members.

07:50.180 --> 07:52.830
But several villagers have been 
killed as an example to others!

07:53.130 --> 07:55.080
We still lack adequate forces.

07:55.080 --> 07:57.820
We should be ready by 
the middle of next month.

07:57.820 --> 07:59.230
You'll have to wait until then.

07:59.230 --> 08:00.530
But...

08:00.950 --> 08:07.500
Why? We've always offered 
prayers to the goddess.

08:07.850 --> 08:10.660
If prayers were enough for 
the goddess to save you,

08:10.660 --> 08:13.200
there wouldn't be adventurers anymore.

08:13.200 --> 08:17.520
The goddess is angry because there 
are more people like you now!

08:18.000 --> 08:20.720
This is why she's so cruel to hyumans!

08:21.280 --> 08:23.690
<i>The goddess's cruelty, huh?</i>

08:23.690 --> 08:27.320
<i>I feel like it's not as bad 
as what she's done to me.</i>

08:27.940 --> 08:32.890
We'd be willing to consider your 
request for a special price.

08:36.120 --> 08:37.170
Move.

08:39.760 --> 08:41.200
Please move.

08:47.950 --> 08:50.180
I knew it.

08:50.520 --> 08:52.940
I shouldn't have paid a whole gold coin.

08:54.360 --> 08:56.600
<i>Three men followed from the tavern,</i>

08:57.040 --> 09:00.060
<i>and four more left the guild.</i>

09:00.320 --> 09:02.550
Eto! Wake up, Eto!

09:02.550 --> 09:06.760
Poor girl. We'll make you feel better.

09:05.940 --> 09:08.060
No! Stop! Let go!

09:08.540 --> 09:11.010
Don't waste your time 
praying to the goddess.

09:11.010 --> 09:12.370
If you're going to pray, pray to someone—

09:14.350 --> 09:15.410
What was that?!

09:19.370 --> 09:22.180
You were at the guild.

09:22.980 --> 09:25.740
A man with a demihuman face 
siding with demihumans?

09:25.740 --> 09:27.950
We'll cut up your ugly fa—

09:32.360 --> 09:36.340
<i>So many hyumans are such scumbags.</i>

09:38.190 --> 09:41.880
<i>Would you allow me to treat him?</i>

09:42.300 --> 09:44.020
Are you a demihuman?

09:44.580 --> 09:46.360
Is that why you're helping us?

09:46.990 --> 09:49.090
<i>Despite my appearance, 
I'm actually a hyuman.</i>

09:49.090 --> 09:51.390
Huh? Wh-What are you doing?

09:51.390 --> 09:52.520
<i>Healing Kai.</i>

09:53.920 --> 09:55.810
What? His wound...

09:56.240 --> 09:59.680
<i>This power I received from 
Tsukuyomi-sama is incredible.</i>

10:00.830 --> 10:02.420
<i>I'm Kuzunoha.</i>

10:02.420 --> 10:05.180
<i>I'm an adventurer, but I work 
primarily as a merchant.</i>

10:05.180 --> 10:08.030
Oh, um... I'm sorry for saying such rude things.

10:08.030 --> 10:09.660
Thank you for helping us.

10:09.660 --> 10:12.780
I'm Lana, from Tapa Village.

10:12.780 --> 10:14.550
This is Eto the werewolf.

10:14.820 --> 10:16.510
<i>A werewolf?</i>

10:16.890 --> 10:19.000
<i>This little furry shota?</i>

10:19.510 --> 10:25.270
<b>How I
\h\h\h\hImagine
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h Werewolves</b>

10:19.510 --> 10:25.270
<b>How I
\h\h\h\hImagine
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h Werewolves</b>

10:19.640 --> 10:23.460
<i>No, I'm sure werewolves come 
in all shapes and sizes.</i>

10:23.460 --> 10:24.660
<i>Please let that be true.</i>

10:24.660 --> 10:25.260
Um?

10:25.840 --> 10:28.300
<i>Oh, sorry. Let me lend you a hand.</i>

10:33.330 --> 10:37.860
<i>By the way, about the Moon over 
the Ruined Castle attacking...</i>

10:37.860 --> 10:39.200
Y-Yes?

10:40.080 --> 10:43.210
<i>Is it true that you can't afford to 
wait for a group to take them out?</i>

10:43.660 --> 10:47.030
They tortured Barkley-san,

10:47.030 --> 10:51.160
the strongest fighter in our village, 
to death as a lesson to us.

10:51.160 --> 10:53.160
They killed his wife, too.

10:53.380 --> 10:55.070
<i>That's awful.</i>

10:55.070 --> 10:59.640
The other villagers say we should comply 
with their demands and hand over our supplies,

11:00.080 --> 11:03.030
but every village they've attacked 
so far has been slaughtered

11:03.030 --> 11:05.860
after having everything taken from them.

11:06.390 --> 11:09.170
Tapa Village is finished.

11:11.430 --> 11:13.290
Eto, are you okay?

11:13.290 --> 11:14.310
Yeah.

11:14.700 --> 11:17.100
So will the guild help us?

11:18.690 --> 11:22.080
I'm sorry. If only I were stronger...

11:23.300 --> 11:26.350
<i>I'm used to death by now.</i>

11:26.350 --> 11:28.860
<i>I've even killed people with my own hands.</i>

11:29.350 --> 11:31.630
<i>Even though it wasn't 
normal in my old world,</i>

11:31.630 --> 11:36.500
<i>I thought I'd accepted that it was 
a common occurrence in this isekai.</i>

11:41.470 --> 11:43.290
<i>I'll escort you to your village.</i>

11:43.290 --> 11:44.390
<i>Where is it?</i>

11:44.390 --> 11:45.030
What?

11:45.030 --> 11:49.810
But our village is near those mountains. 
It takes a long time to get there.

11:50.210 --> 11:51.260
<i>It's okay.</i>

11:52.290 --> 11:54.230
<i>Be careful you don't bite your tongue.</i>

11:54.720 --> 11:56.220
K-Kuzunoha-san?

11:56.220 --> 11:57.690
Wait!

12:00.490 --> 12:05.030
K-Kuzunoha-san, who exactly are you?!

12:05.570 --> 12:07.620
<i>I told you, I'm a merchant.</i>

12:07.620 --> 12:10.500
There's no way that's true!

12:11.970 --> 12:13.600
Wow.

12:13.600 --> 12:15.580
We're already here.

12:15.580 --> 12:18.010
<i>The village is smaller than I expected.</i>

12:18.410 --> 12:21.790
I'd like to thank you. Please wait here.

12:21.790 --> 12:23.890
I'll explain the situation to the villagers.

12:26.890 --> 12:28.440
You're not going to enter the village?

12:28.440 --> 12:30.760
What? You can speak the werewolf language?

12:31.270 --> 12:33.950
Common is the only language I can't speak.

12:34.390 --> 12:37.870
So, you're not from this village?

12:37.870 --> 12:40.480
My village is in the woods over there.

12:41.180 --> 12:44.650
Lana and a few other 
villagers are kind to me,

12:44.650 --> 12:49.810
but most people wouldn't invite a 
demihuman into a hyuman village.

12:49.810 --> 12:51.950
I guess you're right.

12:52.520 --> 12:55.200
But we can't afford to worry 
about that right now.

12:55.540 --> 13:00.150
Kuzunoha-san, is your sense of smell keen 
enough to know what's happening in the village?

13:00.150 --> 13:02.050
So you knew.

13:02.490 --> 13:03.880
<i>Investigative Kai.</i>

13:04.800 --> 13:06.500
I smell blood.

13:06.500 --> 13:08.770
It's not just one or two people, either.

13:08.770 --> 13:11.880
The Moon over the Ruined Castle must've 
made examples of some villagers again.

13:12.660 --> 13:15.230
Seriously, who are you?

13:15.640 --> 13:18.990
I told you, I'm an adventuring merchant.

13:18.990 --> 13:20.690
You certainly don't seem like one.

13:21.000 --> 13:25.740
By the way, you were actually awake 
while I was carrying you, weren't you?

13:25.740 --> 13:26.640
Huh?

13:27.070 --> 13:30.480
You can tell if someone's conscious 
or not by how heavy they feel.

13:30.990 --> 13:35.980
Did you pretend to be asleep because you 
felt bad about putting her in danger?

13:38.200 --> 13:41.570
<i>Whoops. Maybe I sounded a little mean there.</i>

13:42.460 --> 13:46.430
If you want to be with her, then you
 should protect her next time.

13:46.850 --> 13:47.560
Okay.

13:49.660 --> 13:51.500
<i>My Investigative Kai detected something.</i>

13:51.920 --> 13:54.570
I figured they were nearby.

13:54.570 --> 13:55.980
Kuzunoha-san?

13:56.720 --> 13:58.370
I'm going for a walk in the mountains.

13:58.370 --> 14:00.880
But that would be suicide!

14:00.880 --> 14:04.600
So you know what's in the mountains, too.

14:04.600 --> 14:06.160
Wh-Why?

14:06.400 --> 14:09.620
Why are you doing this for us?

14:11.180 --> 14:13.260
"Moon over the Ruined Castle"

14:14.410 --> 14:18.530
is the name of a song from 
a distant land that I liked.

14:19.290 --> 14:23.390
I don't like the idea of dastardly 
bandits using that name.

14:24.000 --> 14:25.500
Is that good enough?

14:27.510 --> 14:30.550
Is there anything I can do?

14:30.550 --> 14:35.170
Well, I have demihumans working 
at my trading company.

14:35.510 --> 14:39.340
If they ever come to 
Tapa Village or your village,

14:39.340 --> 14:41.650
treat them to a delicious meal.

14:44.260 --> 14:49.890
I thought I carefully selected the 
best meat and vegetables, but...

14:48.530 --> 14:50.990
<b></b>Round Two: Tasting Mio's Cooking

14:48.530 --> 14:50.990
<b></b>Round Two: Tasting Mio's Cooking

14:50.990 --> 14:54.490
<b>Lime
Hyuman
(Tomoe's Spy)</b>

14:53.020 --> 14:54.500
<i>I can see the other side...</i>

14:54.490 --> 14:57.200
<b>Agares
 Highland Orc</b>

14:55.400 --> 14:57.190
This is nothing.

14:57.200 --> 15:00.960
<b>Liddy
 Mist Lizard</b>

14:57.520 --> 15:00.580
I can keep fighting.

15:00.960 --> 15:04.670
<b>Akina
 Alke</b>

15:01.230 --> 15:04.660
Unknown flavor, unknown texture...

15:04.660 --> 15:07.420
This time we'll die for sure.

15:04.670 --> 15:10.130
<b>Aqua & Eris & Mondo
Forest Ogres</b>

15:07.420 --> 15:10.120
I can't move.

15:10.120 --> 15:14.020
I thought this might happen, 
so I brought some medicine.

15:14.020 --> 15:15.600
But we're too late.

15:15.830 --> 15:17.280
Why?

15:17.280 --> 15:19.670
Why? You can't be serious.

15:20.090 --> 15:22.600
Komoe, what was today's menu?

15:23.000 --> 15:26.940
Salted chicken skewers 
and orcish vichyssoise.

15:26.940 --> 15:29.400
<b>Mystery Greens Soup</b>

15:26.940 --> 15:29.400
<b>Monster Meat Piccata</b>

15:27.570 --> 15:29.400
These dishes are something else entirely!

15:29.400 --> 15:32.700
I heard the eyes of the potatoes 
used in the soup are poisonous,

15:32.700 --> 15:35.130
but while removing them with the skin...

15:36.020 --> 15:37.270
How?!

15:37.800 --> 15:42.570
These greens cut up the inside of my mouth.

15:42.570 --> 15:45.290
Oh, I picked those in the Wasteland.

15:45.290 --> 15:48.830
Those are killing weeds.

15:48.830 --> 15:54.180
It's a monster with blades for leaves, 
which it uses to slice its prey.

15:54.510 --> 15:56.090
<i>It's a living monster?!</i>

15:56.090 --> 15:58.740
Can they be made delicious?

15:58.740 --> 16:01.760
They can be processed 
into an abrasive paste.

16:02.230 --> 16:04.820
But I'm confident in my meat dish.

16:05.140 --> 16:07.180
I'm sorry, Mio-sama.

16:07.180 --> 16:10.190
No matter what we do, 
we can't bite through it.

16:10.870 --> 16:12.520
Bring it on!

16:13.630 --> 16:16.820
All the strongest warriors 
of each species are dead.

16:16.820 --> 16:18.080
That doesn't make sense.

16:18.490 --> 16:22.830
I used the dishes I previously enjoyed 
with the young master as reference.

16:24.110 --> 16:28.120
Preparing monster meat must 
require special techniques.

16:28.480 --> 16:31.750
This oil is hephais oil.

16:31.750 --> 16:34.090
It's a rare lubricating oil.

16:34.400 --> 16:36.040
Lubricating oil?

16:36.040 --> 16:37.570
You mean...

16:37.570 --> 16:39.300
It's for industrial use?!

16:39.300 --> 16:40.500
Grease!

16:40.870 --> 16:43.980
I only participated because 
I sensed bananas.

16:43.980 --> 16:45.440
<b>Banana Garnish (Covered in Oil)</b>

16:45.430 --> 16:48.410
How could you kill these bananas?!

16:50.860 --> 16:52.940
I won't be beaten.

16:54.190 --> 16:56.570
You served fruit as garnish for meat?

16:56.570 --> 16:59.270
There was a restaurant that served 
a delicious dish like that.

16:59.690 --> 17:02.270
I heard sweet and sour pork 
contains fruit, as well.

17:02.270 --> 17:03.740
That's a different fruit!

17:04.250 --> 17:08.720
Good ingredients don't guarantee 
the cooked dish will be delicious,

17:08.720 --> 17:12.490
especially since different species have 
varying senses of taste and preferences.

17:12.840 --> 17:15.000
I prefer raw foods.

17:15.000 --> 17:16.650
I prefer salty dishes.

17:16.650 --> 17:19.200
Bananas! Bananas!

17:19.200 --> 17:21.090
I like persimmons!

17:21.090 --> 17:25.430
C-Cooking is so complex...

17:25.430 --> 17:28.470
If you're cooking to suit 
the young master's tastes,

17:28.470 --> 17:31.320
then asking Lime for his opinion 
as another hyuman would be best.

17:31.320 --> 17:32.320
Me?!

17:32.320 --> 17:35.980
That said, the burden would 
be too much for him alone,

17:36.110 --> 17:37.280
<b>Desperate Times Call for Desperate Measures</b>

17:36.290 --> 17:37.270
so I have an idea.

17:37.490 --> 17:42.980
You'll travel the world to gain insights on 
the fundamentals of cooking and ingredients.

17:42.980 --> 17:44.240
How does that sound?

17:44.950 --> 17:48.220
Tomoe-san, you...

17:49.380 --> 17:51.120
<i>She doesn't like the idea.</i>

17:51.440 --> 17:54.190
You have such fantastic ideas!

17:54.190 --> 17:55.890
Right?

17:56.290 --> 17:58.840
<i>Oh, good.</i>

17:59.070 --> 18:02.010
I shall travel the land 
honing my cooking skills

18:02.010 --> 18:04.220
so that I can please the young master!

18:05.690 --> 18:06.640
Good, good!

18:06.200 --> 18:08.680
<i>I must hurry with my own investigation.</i>

18:09.210 --> 18:13.140
<i>I can't allow the young master to 
get dragged into any more trouble.</i>

18:15.910 --> 18:17.740
What are the villagers doing?

18:17.740 --> 18:19.570
They're collecting money.

18:19.570 --> 18:22.090
They should just hand it over already.

18:22.090 --> 18:24.600
How many can we kill today?

18:24.600 --> 18:26.550
Let's raise some hell.

18:27.020 --> 18:31.510
<i>I never thought I'd wear this again, but 
I don't want them to figure out who I am.</i>

18:32.110 --> 18:34.420
<i>Finally, Silencing Kai.</i>

18:44.930 --> 18:47.210
<i>What's going on? I can't speak.</i>

18:47.680 --> 18:50.700
<i>No, all sounds have disappeared!</i>

18:52.080 --> 18:52.880
<i>Wha—</i>

18:53.280 --> 18:55.230
<i>We're under attack?!</i>

18:55.630 --> 18:57.060
<i>Sheesh.</i>

18:58.000 --> 19:01.070
<i>I said I didn't want to get too 
deeply involved with hyumans,</i>

19:01.490 --> 19:04.240
<i>but here I am exterminating 
bandits for them.</i>

19:04.240 --> 19:08.210
<i>But I decided to follow my heart 
when I'm not sure what to do.</i>

19:13.320 --> 19:14.670
<i>It's him.</i>

19:15.460 --> 19:17.420
<i>I'm not shooting to kill.</i>

19:17.420 --> 19:19.380
<i>My arrows are enchanted to 
knock them out, though.</i>

19:19.380 --> 19:20.590
<i>Die!</i>

19:21.700 --> 19:24.260
<i>You can always count on 
Elder Dwarf equipment.</i>

19:24.260 --> 19:25.940
<i>Its defense is fantastic.</i>

19:26.770 --> 19:28.880
<i>Anyway, why must there 
be so many of them?</i>

19:29.780 --> 19:31.640
<i>I don't want to waste my arrows.</i>

19:34.620 --> 19:39.620
<i>When Emma-san first taught me, 
I wasn't sure if I'd be able to master it.</i>

19:42.250 --> 19:44.400
<i>But I've gotten totally used to it.</i>

19:45.750 --> 19:47.250
The sound is back.

19:47.250 --> 19:49.750
<i>This arrow won't miss.</i>

19:50.710 --> 19:51.320
Whoa!

20:07.010 --> 20:08.260
S-Spare me!

20:08.910 --> 20:12.420
<i>I won't kill you, but before I go...</i>

20:13.090 --> 20:16.430
<i>Don't call yourselves the Moon over 
the Ruined Castle ever again.</i>

20:25.830 --> 20:27.230
What happened here?

20:27.500 --> 20:28.890
What happened to them?

20:28.890 --> 20:30.700
Does this mean we're saved?

20:30.700 --> 20:32.740
S-Someone contact the adventurer's guild!

20:31.750 --> 20:33.260
Was this...

20:32.740 --> 20:34.150
Transport the wounded!

20:33.260 --> 20:34.150
Yeah.

20:34.410 --> 20:36.830
So our prayers were heard.

20:43.800 --> 20:46.590
Young Master, where have you been?

20:46.590 --> 20:48.260
Out.

20:48.670 --> 20:50.010
I see.

20:51.170 --> 20:53.970
More importantly, did you find an inn?

20:53.970 --> 20:59.170
Yes. I can finally escort 
you to a passable inn.

20:59.170 --> 21:00.980
It costs three gold coins per night.

21:01.280 --> 21:04.340
Three gold coins is 30,000 yen.

21:04.870 --> 21:06.200
Don't you think that's too expensive?

21:06.480 --> 21:11.170
By the way, I heard the 
so-called heroes are treated

21:11.170 --> 21:16.630
quite hospitably by the Limia 
Kingdom and Gritonia Empire.

21:16.630 --> 21:18.080
What? Really?

21:18.470 --> 21:24.460
As your follower, I cannot allow you to be 
the only one forced to live in poverty.

21:24.830 --> 21:26.150
Is that right?

21:29.760 --> 21:31.220
<i>Heroes, huh?</i>

21:31.820 --> 21:35.730
I've found other heroes 
suitable for my world.

21:38.260 --> 21:42.180
<i>They were apparently present at the 
battlefield I was thrown into before.</i>

21:42.600 --> 21:46.240
<i>I wonder when I'll run into them.</i>

21:53.740 --> 21:55.090
<i>Somewhere in this world</i>

21:55.090 --> 21:56.420
<i>Are a couple of heroes</i>

21:56.420 --> 21:57.910
<i>But where could they be?</i>

21:58.600 --> 22:01.680
<i>Misumi Makoto, </i>Poems of the Heart<i>.</i>

23:36.180 --> 23:39.870
<i>Night Two: "The Heroes Are 
a Couple of Beauties."</i>

23:36.390 --> 23:40.010
<b>Next Time</b>

23:37.390 --> 23:40.010
<b>The Heroes Are a Couple of Beauties</b>
